  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The centre turn – 3v3 in lanes",
  "description": "A 3v3 game with goalies on an area of about 20 × 20 metres, for example half the rink with an extra net at the red line. Cones split the area into three lanes running from the end boards to the red line. Each player has a fixed position in one lane.\n\nA goal only counts if the puck has been passed at least once from an outer lane into the middle one. This makes the team use the width and gives the centre lots of chances to receive, turn and shoot.\n\nProgression: play freely without fixed positions, but keep the rule about the pass from an outer to the middle lane.\n\nNot to scale. The goalies are not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Centre: skate so you are available whenever the puck is in an outer lane."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Receive with your body open towards the net so you can turn quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Wingers: keep the width so there is space in the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Defence: how can you stop the puck being switched from one outer lane to the other?"
    }
  ],
